cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Matched permutation nulls for certified worst-case intervals in spatial
  co-expression
message: >-
  If you use this code or the certified-interval construction, please cite the
  accompanying manuscript and this repository.
authors:
  - given-names: Amy
    family-names: Wang
version: 1.0.4
date-released: "2026-10-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/amywang2010/lr-certificates"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Per-contrast intervals for a co-expression score in spatial transcriptomics,
  valid over a declared set of molecule-to-cell reassignments (boundary-local
  reassignment with per-cell gain and loss capacity constraints, mask erosion
  and dilation, and a parameterised donor radius). Each interval end is the
  optimum of a capacitated matching between boundary transcripts and cells,
  relaxed in the released code to a linear-time count. A permutation null that
  recomputes the same worst-case object under every label permutation yields
  exact finite-B p-values, and any null that holds the assignment fixed is
  proved dominated. A claim requires the interval to exclude zero and the
  matched null to confirm the direction, with the direction read from the
  interval absorbed by the Benjamini-Yekutieli factor. Evaluated on three public
  Xenium sections spanning two tissues, two panel densities and two tumour types.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - molecule reassignment
  - matched permutation null
  - worst-case intervals
  - capacitated matching
  - selective inference
